{
  "note": "Expected values read off the Figma file 'Rancher Extension Studio - AI Authoring (Concept)' (Xm3Q6WVin7U3cwMeOdGV6z). Each entry names the node it came from, plus the style id from the globalVars block of the fetch that produced it. NOTE ON STYLE IDS: the MCP layout_*/fill_*/stroke_* ids are generated per response, not stable across fetches, so they identify the value inside one dump rather than across the file - the node id is the durable half of the citation. Colours are the light-theme literals. Where the extension routes a colour through a Rancher shell variable, the expectation is still the Figma literal: the two used to agree because the shell variables were unset in the scope the tokens were declared in, and they no longer do (see README of the defect report).",
  "conventions": {
    "pad": "top right bottom left, px, no units",
    "gap": "single number when both axes match, else row/column",
    "size": "WxH; '*' means unconstrained on that axis",
    "font": "px/weight",
    "border": "top right bottom left widths",
    "from": "<figma node id> <style id> - the node the number was read off"
  },
  "unexpressible": [
    "Status-fill foregrounds (.s-tab__count on 03-workspace 11:212 and 05-files 22:916, the 11-queue selected pill 36:1061, the verdict segments 39:1233 and the verification badges): Figma writes #FFFFFF on every one. Not followed. All five carry 11-12px/600, which WCAG counts as normal text needing 4.5:1, and white fails on all of them - success #3E8C4F 4.14, error #F64747 5.42 light but #FF6B6B 2.78 dark, warning #C9A227 2.42 light and #E0BC4A 1.83 dark. The app uses --studio-on-status (#0E0E12), which clears every one: 4.65 / 5.42 / 6.94 / 7.96 / 10.51. #141419, the body ink, was tried first and is not enough - 4.43 on the green, just under the line. Deliberate departure on accessibility grounds, not a defect.\n\nDeliberately NOT extended to .s-btn--primary and .s-btn--danger. Those are 14px/600 on the same fills and fail the same way, but a primary button is host chrome: Rancher ships white-on-green primaries, and dark-inked ones would read as broken beside them. The token sheet's stated rule is that Rancher wins on host-consistent surfaces. Recorded as a known gap rather than silently fixed.",
    "Rancher's own chrome (nav rail, header) is out of scope.",
    ".new-ext__prompt border colour: Figma 13:313 strokes 2px #3D98D3, but the app routes it through --studio-border-focus -> Rancher --outline, which is #008657 in Prime light. Deferring a focus colour to the host product is the stated rule in studio.css, so only the 2px width is checked.",
    "03-workspace assistant pane width: --studio-panel-assistant is 520px, but editor.vue seeds the splitter from localStorage \"barn.editor.split\" (a percentage) and only falls back to the token when that key is absent. Any profile that has dragged the divider renders a different width forever, so a pane-width expectation would measure the harness browser's history rather than the design. The 520 is checked by reading the token, not the box.",
    {
      "selector": "11-queue .s-tab__count color",
      "figma": "36:1061 Caption/11 SemiBold Caps fill #FFFFFF",
      "why": "Deliberate departure, on accessibility grounds. The pill is 11px/600 - normal text by WCAG, needing 4.5:1 - and the frame's white on the #3E8C4F fill is 4.14:1. The app uses --studio-on-success (#0E0E12) at 4.65:1. The same call was already made for the amber pill on 03/05; this is the last surface of the same family. Not a defect."
    }
  ],
