        },
        ".verify__verdicts > *": {
          "size": "71x30",
          "from": "39:1233 layout_2QJM52 - the segment is horizontal-fill/vertical-fill inside the 216x30 control 39:1232 (as the original entry already recorded), not a fixed 72. Three FILL children share the CONTENT box of the 216x30 control 39:1232, and that control carries a 1px stroke, so the content box is 214x28 and a segment is 214/3 = 71.33 wide. 72 was the spec's own arithmetic (216/3) and it is wrong for a border-box: 3x72 overflows the container by 2px. The measure rounds, so a correct implementation reads 71. Height stays 30 because the segments are pulled over the horizontal border with negative margins; only the width overflows. Live symptom, which the number alone does not convey: because 3x72 overflows the 214px content box, the control is a scroll container. Clicking the third segment scrolls it 2px, which clips \"Yes\" and eats the right-hand border on that row only, and the shift is sticky - toggling the verdict back off does not undo it. Fix is flex: 1 1 0 on the segment (and dropping the negative margins, which overflow:hidden clips at the padding box and so never paint)."
        }
      }
